AUDIO: 'might make it a little bit smoother. But, the other thing is that this setup doesn\'t magically make a better output. Like if you think like these four agents and they\'re all in agreement and there\'s no friction, you\'re just going to have four agents nodding at each other the entire time. We\'ve all seen that with'

[08:00] [scene:analysis]
VISUAL: The creator continues discussing the importance of agent roles and avoiding "yes-men" behavior.
AUDIO: 'like the front-facing consumer version of ChatGPT where it\'s just like the biggest yes-man that that ever was, you know, you\'ll give it some stupid idea and it says "You\'re the best." So, that\'s like super not helpful. You need friction and you need conflict. These'

[08:12] [scene:talk]
